## Step 3: the open point on FR-6 (task item 3)

FR-6 says a `word` card "appears in the text of an earlier day of the same week, or in the text of an earlier week". No section defines "the text of a day". The author reads it as the English lines of the day's steps. Decision: yes, this leaves an implementer decision open. The check author must decide which strings count: the English lines of the day's steps only, or also the prep lines, the Thai lines, or the reader page text of the day's read-along. The readings give different pass sets for `loops-recall`. The plan repeats the phrase in its word-card test cases, so the plan does not close it either. Classification: Major (an undefined project-specific term that decides the check result), consistent with round 1 F3 and F5. Finding F10 records it. The fix is one sentence in FR-6, or the user accepts the ambiguity.

